                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c64468d2-1945-45e5-a36b-e43a7b6f6bda",
                        "entry_id": "b01ccb84-c0e9-391b-a171-a6a8ca328ba5",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "slunks"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9cec68b8-df8b-3c18-a070-633b4f84019e",
                        "entry_id": "b01ccb84-c0e9-391b-a171-a6a8ca328ba5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An animal, especially a calf, born prematurely or abortively."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "28ce7da9-9956-4063-8ef3-5462dd2efed6",
                                "sense_id": "9cec68b8-df8b-3c18-a070-633b4f84019e",
                                "text": "Then I met a great guy, Placenta Juan the Afterbirth Tycoon. Made his in slunks during the war. (Slunks are underage calves trailing afterbirths and bacteria, generally in an unsanitary and unfit condition.)"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "94a61c8a-26fb-49ab-86e0-880acefa1a2d",
                                "sense_id": "9cec68b8-df8b-3c18-a070-633b4f84019e",
                                "text": "Calf heads were tanned from yearling calves less than a year in age. Slunk skins were tanned from unborn calfskins which, gruesome as it sounds, were often by products of the cow slaughtering process."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "b2a43027-84ad-3868-81aa-c6dff5d4ad5d",
                "word": "slunk",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "53d4c66e-36b1-407f-bc34-3f21bb8b5f1e",
                        "entry_id": "b2a43027-84ad-3868-81aa-c6dff5d4ad5d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "slunks"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dce7d182-950b-37c2-98d9-e75ec378e385",
                        "entry_id": "b2a43027-84ad-3868-81aa-c6dff5d4ad5d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A slough, a low, wet, miry place. (Compare slank.)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "UK",
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea4f4412-8de6-4844-b924-510648ed8d03",
                                "sense_id": "dce7d182-950b-37c2-98d9-e75ec378e385",
                                "text": "Amang the harbour's sludge and mud; They row'd thegither in the slunk; Their heads were up, their bodies sunk; What wi' the slusch they ate and drunk, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1747f5ac-e12b-48a4-aee7-f34dd85c23ff",
                                "sense_id": "dce7d182-950b-37c2-98d9-e75ec378e385",
                                "text": "He made the road, and since it was made there was never anything done to it except when men were carting turf and then they would fill in a \"slunk.\" You might say now it is no road."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7858cd57-376b-4e7c-932c-659078b22008",
                                "sense_id": "dce7d182-950b-37c2-98d9-e75ec378e385",
                                "text": "[…] a 'slunk' is a 'slonk' (depression) with mud; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
